        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:22:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63026,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>JA01.Z Ectopic pregnancy, unspecified</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:22:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63027,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> deciduosis; decidualized endometriosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:22:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63028,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:22:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63029,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "<p>By definition, this occurs outside the uterine body {26926901}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-19T16:08:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63030,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ectopic decidua is usually an asymptomatic, incidental finding {28351025; 12068174}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:22:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63031,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "<p>Ectopic decidua usually occurs in women of reproductive age. Microscopically, it occurs in all women during pregnancy; macroscopically, it can be seen in as many as 10% of pregnant women {26717495}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-19T16:08:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63032,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It occurs during pregnancy or progestin use.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:22:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63033,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It probably originates from decidualization in endometriosis. In addition, it could arise in decidual metaplasia of subserosal mesenchymal cells or lymphatic dissemination of endometrial cells {26926901}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:22:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63034,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ectopic decidua presents as single or multiple small nodules of variable colour, 0.2&ndash;2&nbsp;cm in size {26717495}. Rarely, it can be larger {26926901}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:22:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63035,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is solid growth of polygonal&nbsp;/ focally spindled cells with well-delineated borders; eosinophilic, basophilic, or amphophilic cytoplasm; and nuclei with fine chromatin and prominent nucleoli. Necrosis, low mitotic activity, signet-ring cells, focal nuclear pleomorphism, and hyperchromasia can be seen. Immunohistochemical studies show that the cells are positive for ER and PR and typically negative for keratin and calretinin {26717495; 26926901}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:22:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63036,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:22:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63037,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:22:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63038,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> nodules of decidualized cells outside the uterine body.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-19T16:08:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
